  "fields": {
    "title": "Framework",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "A framework refers to a programming framework, which are used in software technology and espacially webdevelopment. In a more general sense, a framework is also used to describe an organisational framework. A framework is not a finished programme itself, but provides the frame in which a programmer creates an application, whereby the structure of the individual application is influenced by the development patterns used in the framework. A framework is a library that offers opinions about how software gets built. These opinions allow for predictability and homogeneity in an application. Predictability allows the software to scale to an enormous size and still be maintainable, which is quite useful when many developers are writing a software or website together. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6lD0NRqIKlsz3HtTqYS2KO",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "There are a lot of different frameworks today, that try to make coding complex applications simpler. Even tho most websites these days are built with frameworks,  you don't need to use a framework when building a website. Especially if you are just learning to code or are only building a simple site, using a framework may only complicate your work instead of simplifying it. This website was built using the javascript framework svelte.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "When JavaScript debuted in 1996, it added occasional interactivity and excitement to a web that was, up until then, composed of static documents. The web became not just a place to ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "read things",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", but to ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "do things",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". JavaScript's popularity steadily increased. Developers who worked with JavaScript wrote tools to solve the problems they faced, and packaged them into reusable packages called libraries, so they could share their solutions with others. This shared ecosystem of libraries helped shape the growth of the web. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6lD0NRqIKlsz3HtTqYS2KO",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
